+## Keys and roles
+
+Requests carry `Authorization: Bearer <key>`. Keys are in the data as
+`apiKeys: [{ "key", "name", "role" }]`.
+
+- `viewer`: reads (GET) only.
+- `cook`: also cooks recipes, records waste, logs temperatures and enters
+  stock-take counts (`POST /stocktakes/:id/counts`).
+- `manager`: everything, including `GET /audit`.
+
+No key or an unknown key: 401 `unauthorized`. A known key without
+permission: 403 `forbidden`. Every changing (non-GET) request by a known key
+is written to the audit trail (time, key name, method, path, status);
+`GET /audit` lists it newest first.
+
